					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-465826#post-1436674</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-465826/scp-5200-j#post-1436674</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 03 May 2012 16:58:55 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>genesplicer</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>558043</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This particular SCP is primarily combated in middle school science/health classes. Every year my district sends me a new program to help the kids fight. Every year it seems become more and more out of touch with the kids. In the last set, there were videos (Updated last year) that showed two of the cool kids who avoid drugs were dressed like a cross between Kid N Play and the Gangsters from Michael Jackson's &quot;Bad&quot;. And this was the updated video clips. It's amazing we haven't been overrun and destroyed by this SCP&#8230;</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-465826#post-1436645</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-465826/scp-5200-j#post-1436645</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 03 May 2012 16:38:12 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>tombones</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>398766</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Yeah, unfortunately. &quot;Just say no&quot; became a bland, overdone punchline within days of its introduction, and all this -J does is regurgitate it for the kids who weren't around to get tired of it.</p> <p>This could be funny if it presented those naive health class antidrug slogans in a suitably grave, clinical tone, as if they would actually be effective. &quot;In the event of a breach, personnel should speak Defensive Phrase 5200-A (&quot;No&quot;) aloud until containment is reestablished&quot; or something along those lines. As it stands, it's just &quot;Hey, remember the 90s? Remember DARE?? Haha!&quot; which does it for some people, apparently, but isn't exactly comedy.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
